#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# The frame pump, as a stream edge -- the exact shape window_events.etcs
# already uses for input, applied to output.
#
# REQUIRES a module change that is not on main yet: Surface must become
# ETCS_TAG_BLOCK_HYBRID with a ProduceFrames/ConsumeFrames pair. Until then
# use render_script.etcs, which drives frames from Surface.RunDemo on the
# script's own thread instead.
#
# The split is the same one the input edge makes, read in the other
# direction. ProduceFrames owns TIMING and acquisition: it acquires the next
# swapchain image and emits one frame token per acquire, non-blocking, on a
# pool worker. ConsumeFrames owns RECORDING: it takes each token, records
# clear + pending draws into that frame's command buffer, submits, presents,
# and blocks holding the edge open for as long as the surface lives.
#
# Neither side touches PollEvents -- that stays with whoever created the
# window (render_script_streamed.etcs's own thread). This is the whole point
# of moving the frame loop here: Vulkan is happy to submit and present from
# a thread that did not create the window, GLFW is not happy to be polled
# from one that did not.

requires view [Surface]

view.ProduceFrames() -> view.ConsumeFrames()
